WEBVTT

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.795
So now we can use
the input to rotate the

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:11.081
bolt, we're going to translate
this to creating some movement.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.183
We'll go back into our player
controller script here and you

00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:17.640
can see that we'll start
adjusting this to make it happen.

00:00:17.641 --> 00:00:21.260
The rotation speed that we had,
we can rename this to a player

00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:25.000
speed just to make this more
suitable for what we're going to use.

00:00:25.001 --> 00:00:29.440
We're going to also want a reference to
our rigid body that's on our player to make

00:00:29.441 --> 00:00:32.680
it show that we can cause it to
have some forces to make it move.

00:00:32.779 --> 00:00:36.560
Underneath that input system variable, we'll
have another private variable, it's going

00:00:36.561 --> 00:00:39.672
to be type rigid body
and we're going to give

00:00:39.684 --> 00:00:42.600
this a name of player
RB with a semicolon.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.120
So then we can use this.

00:00:44.121 --> 00:00:49.400
We also do need to make sure that we find
it in a wake to cache the reference because

00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:52.440
it's great to just do this once
before everything initializes.

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:56.109
So we'll say player RB
equals get component

00:00:56.121 --> 00:00:59.660
and then in the angle
brackets left and right

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:01.691
we'll have rigid body,
the parentheses and

00:01:01.703 --> 00:01:05.440
the semicolon because we're just
finding that component that we need.

00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:07.574
Now in the side, the update
method where we had the move

00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:11.760
input, the forward input
and the transform dot rotate.

00:01:11.761 --> 00:01:15.000
In this case, we don't want
transform dot rotate anymore.

00:01:15.001 --> 00:01:19.480
We can just rename this and we can use
something different so we'll say player RB is

00:01:19.481 --> 00:01:22.544
what we can use and we'll say
dot add force because we want to

00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:26.880
force the right to body with
some elements of force in that.

00:01:26.881 --> 00:01:29.058
So to move it forward,
we'll use another vector

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.120
three, but instead of
up, we'll use a vector

00:01:31.121 --> 00:01:35.600
three dot forward because we want to push
it in that direction and instead of having

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:41.160
a comma here, we're going to times that
by the forward input that we already had.

00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:44.373
Then we multiply the
rotation speed, but we

00:01:44.385 --> 00:01:47.760
also need to get the
player speed and replace

00:01:47.761 --> 00:01:53.560
that so it's multiplied the player
speed, multiplied by time dot delta time.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:55.120
Then we can save this out.

00:01:55.121 --> 00:01:57.073
Now our player has the
rigid body and the play

00:01:57.085 --> 00:01:59.881
controller with the player
speed of around 150.

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:02.446
If we test this out, we
can move S to move

00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:05.120
backwards and then
double you to move forwards.

00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:07.257
It is a little bit
unresponsive so I like to

00:02:07.269 --> 00:02:11.760
put the player speed up to around 1000 and
then we get a more of a responsive take on

00:02:11.772 --> 00:02:14.400
the movement forward
and backward and you can

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.823
up the mass and adjust
any of the drag settings

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:21.120
if you want this to feel slightly different
when you're controlling your character.

00:02:21.121 --> 00:02:23.838
So what I want you to
do is go to your player

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.640
controller script and
rename the public float,

00:02:26.641 --> 00:02:29.095
which was rotation speed
to player speed, make

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:33.240
sure you add a private variable
rigid body and call this player happy.

00:02:33.241 --> 00:02:37.000
In the awake method, make sure player
happy is equal to the get components.

00:02:37.001 --> 00:02:40.600
We need to initialize
and find the component.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:46.720
Then down in the update method, we make
sure that we're using then player rigid body

00:02:46.721 --> 00:02:49.515
dot add force and it's
going to be vector 3

00:02:49.527 --> 00:02:52.400
dot forward times by
the forward input times

00:02:52.401 --> 00:02:56.600
by player speed and
times by time dot delta time.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:03:00.240
And then you can come back into unity at
just any of your rigid body settings and you

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:11.640
play controller player
speed and test it out.